#!/bin/sh
# Prints how to work inside a Dockerbox agent box.
cat <<'TXT'
Dockerbox - you are root inside an isolated box.

  Persistent:  /root and /workspace (kept when the box is re-created)
  Network:     Internet via the egress proxy (HTTP/HTTPS). Host, LAN and
               other agents are not reachable by design.
  Session:     this console is a tmux session; closing the browser keeps it
               running. Detach: Ctrl-b d   New window: Ctrl-b c

Install an agent (examples, check the vendor's docs for current commands):
  apt-get update && apt-get install -y nodejs npm python3 python3-pip
  npm install -g <agent-cli-package>
  pip install --break-system-packages <agent-package>
  curl -fsSL <vendor-install-script-url> | bash

SSH through the proxy (e.g. git over SSH):
  ssh -o ProxyCommand='nc -X connect -x dockerbox-egress:3128 %h %p' git@github.com
  (or use HTTPS remotes, which use the proxy automatically)

API keys you store here are readable by the agent in this box.
Use dedicated keys with spending limits.
TXT
